course: dictionary
lesson: 8265
title: Ridge: a long line that is raised up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A ridge is a long, narrow line that stands up above what is around it. Read the words near it to find out what kind of ridge it is. «Most of the Earth's volcanic activity happens unseen on the ocean floor along mid-ocean ridges.» The word along tells you a ridge is a long line, not a single spot.
explain: «Cardboard is made by running paper through hot ridged rollers to make a wavy layer.» Ridged is the clue. Rollers with ridges have raised lines on them, so a ridge is a raised line on a surface.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does «a long, narrow, high strip along the top of the hills» fit? Yes, so that is one meaning. Does «raised lines on the rollers» fit? Yes, that is another. The sentence tells you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: A ridge can be a long, narrow, high strip of land along the top of hills or mountains.
fact: A ridge can be a raised line on a surface, like the ridges on the edge of a coin.
fact: The ridge of a roof is the top edge where two sloping parts meet.
fact: «Fingerprints are ridges that help us grip», and every person's are different, even identical twins'.
fact: A weather ridge is a long area of high air pressure.
exercise: «Most of the Earth's volcanic activity happens unseen on the ocean floor along mid-ocean ridges.» Where does this activity happen? | In the sky above the clouds | *On the ocean floor, along the ridges | Inside a kitchen oven | On top of the tallest tree
exercise: Find and copy the one word in «Cardboard is made by running paper through hot ridged rollers» that tells you the rollers have raised lines. | *ridged | running | paper | cardboard
exercise: Which is a ridge on a crisp? | A dry crumb that falls off | A hole right through the middle | *A raised line on its surface | A soft, sticky spot
test: Ridge means a long, narrow, high strip of land. Which picture fits best? | A flat beach beside the sea | A deep hole in the ground | A small pond in a field | *A long line of mountains along the top of the hills
test: Fingerprints are called ridges. What do they help us do? | Swim faster | See in the dark | *Grip things | Hear sounds from far away
exam: Ridge can also mean a weather pattern. What is a ridge of high pressure? | *A long area of high air pressure | Cold water under the ice | Storm clouds that fall as rain | A river running down a hill
